#: ../../../build/NEWS:54
msgid ""
":gh:`158446`: Fix a crash or incorrect output that could occur when "
"formatting a :class:`float` or :class:`complex` with a precision close to "
"the platform's ``INT_MAX``.  :c:func:`PyOS_double_to_string` now "
"raises :exc:`ValueError` for any precision of that magnitude, regardless of "
"presentation type or value, as the format string parsers already did for "
"precisions above ``INT_MAX``."
msgstr ""
":gh:`158446`: プラットフォームの ``INT_MAX`` に近い精度で :class:`float` "
"や :class:`complex` を書式化すると、クラッシュしたり誤った出力を生成したりす"
"る問題を修正しました。\n"
":c:func:`PyOS_double_to_string` は、この程度に大きな精度に対して、表現型や値"
"にかかわらず :exc:`ValueError` を送出するようになりました。\n"
"これは、書式文字列のパーサーがすでに ``INT_MAX`` を超える精度に対して行ってい"
"た動作です。"

#: ../../../build/NEWS:61
msgid ""
":gh:`156793`: :mod:`asyncio`: :meth:`loop.start_tls() "
"<asyncio.loop.start_tls>` and :meth:`loop.create_connection() "
"<asyncio.loop.create_connection>` now validate the *server_hostname* "
"argument if an :class:`ssl.SSLContext` is passed with *check_hostname* set "
"to ``True``, emitting :exc:`DeprecationWarning` if *server_hostname* is "
"missing. (This will raise :exc:`ValueError` in Python 3.13 and later.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:68
msgid ""
":gh:`156793`: :meth:`ssl.SSLContext.wrap_bio` now validates its "
"*server_side*, *server_hostname* and *session* arguments similar "
"to :meth:`ssl.SSLContext.wrap_socket`, but for backward compatiblity reasons "
"emits :exc:`DeprecationWarning` instead of :exc:`ValueError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:73
msgid ""
"In particular, a context with :attr:`~ssl.SSLContext.check_hostname` enabled "
"and no *server_hostname* passed to :meth:`!wrap_bio` now "
"emits :exc:`DeprecationWarning` to indicate the hostname wasn't checked. (In "
"Python 3.13 and later, this raises :exc:`ValueError`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:78
msgid ""
":gh:`157265`: In :mod:`tarfile`, when extracting a link falls back to "
"extracting a member of the archive, skip the member when the filter function "
"returns None when called with the extracted member's name replaced with the "
"link's."
msgstr ""
":gh:`157265`: :mod:`tarfile` でリンクの展開からアーカイブのメンバーの展開に"
"フォールバックする際、展開対象のメンバー名をリンク名に置き換えて呼び出した"
"フィルター関数が None を返した場合、そのメンバーをスキップするようにしまし"
"た。"

#: ../../../build/NEWS:83
msgid ""
":gh:`157190`: Fixed a vulnerability in the :mod:`tarfile` ``data`` and "
"``tar`` extraction filters where a crafted archive using a hard link to a "
"symbolic link could change the permissions and modification time of a file "
"outside the destination directory, and expose its contents inside the "
"extracted tree. This addresses CVE 2026-82049."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:89
msgid ""
":gh:`157953`: Update bundled `libexpat <https://libexpat.github.io/>`_ to "
"version 2.8.5."
msgstr ""
":gh:`157953`: 同梱の `libexpat <https://libexpat.github.io/>`_ をバージョン "
"2.8.5 に更新しました。"

#: ../../../build/NEWS:92
msgid ""
":gh:`156002`: Bound the amount of data :mod:`zipfile` decompresses per read "
"for members compressed with bzip2, LZMA, or Zstandard, matching the existing "
"limit for deflate. A small archive member could previously expand into an "
"unbounded allocation even when read in small chunks."
msgstr ""
":gh:`156002`: bzip2、LZMA、Zstandard で圧縮されたメンバーについ"
"て、:mod:`zipfile` が 1 回の読み取りで展開するデータ量に、deflate に対する既"
"存の制限と同様の上限を設けました。\n"
"以前は小さなアーカイブメンバーを小さいチャンクで読み取っていても、展開時に際"
"限なくメモリーが割り当てられることがありました。"

#: ../../../build/NEWS:97
msgid ""
":gh:`155999`: Fix the :mod:`tarfile` ``tar`` and ``data`` extraction filters "
"creating directories outside the destination for members whose name leaves "
"the destination and returns to it, such as ``../evil/../dest/sub/file``. The "
"containment check used the resolved path, but intermediate directories were "
"created from the name as given."
msgstr ""
":gh:`155999`: ``../evil/../dest/sub/file`` のように展開先から外れて再び戻る名"
"前のメンバーに対して、:mod:`tarfile` の ``tar`` および ``data`` 展開フィル"
"ターが展開先の外にディレクトリを作成する問題を修正しました。\n"
"包含関係の検査には解決済みのパスを使用していましたが、中間ディレクトリの作成"
"には指定されたままの名前を使用していました。"

#: ../../../build/NEWS:103
msgid ""
":gh:`156293`: Fix a crash in :mod:`ssl` when "
"an :attr:`~ssl.SSLContext.sni_callback` switches a connection to "
"another :class:`~ssl.SSLContext` and the context that carries the callback "
"is no longer referenced by the application. Servers that keep their "
"``sni_callback`` context alive (the usual case when it wraps the listening "
"socket or is stored on the server object) were not affected. This addresses "
"`:cve:`2026-19445` <https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=:cve:`2026-19445`>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:112
msgid ""
":gh:`155292`: Change the :mod:`stringprep` module and :mod:`encodings.idna` "
"codec to not consider Unicode codepoint attributes beyond those defined "
"in :rfc:`3454`."
msgstr ""
":gh:`155292`: :mod:`stringprep` モジュールと :mod:`encodings.idna` codec "
"が、:rfc:`3454` に定義されたもの以外の Unicode コードポイントの属性を考慮しな"
"いように変更しました。"

#: ../../../build/NEWS:116
msgid ""
":gh:`155694`: Fix `:cve:`2026-15806` <https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?"
"id=:cve:`2026-15806`>`_ by scoping :class:`~urllib.request.HTTPPasswordMgr` "
"credentials to the URL scheme, preventing credentials stored for an HTTPS "
"URL from being used for a matching HTTP URL, while URIs without a scheme "
"continue to match any scheme."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:126
msgid ""
":gh:`156002`: :mod:`zipfile` again reads members through a third-party "
"decompressor installed by monkey-patching the private "
"``_get_decompressor()`` to return an object that only implements old "
"BZ2Decompressor API from Python 3.3. Note that decompressors without "
"``needs_input`` and two-argument ``decompress()`` are vulnerable to CVE "
"2026-15310."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../build/NEWS:133
msgid ""
":gh:`156353`: Fix :mod:`configparser` parsing when using whitespace in "
"*delimiters*."
msgstr ""
":gh:`156353`: *delimiters* に空白を使用した場合の :mod:`configparser` の解析"
"を修正しました。"

